  "live_records": {
    "q-97634": {
      "dom_id": "step-q97634",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "A particle moves along a circular path centered at $O$ in the $xy$-plane in the counterclockwise direction with a constant angular velocity of $\\frac{1}{4}\\text{ rad/s}.$ Given that the object is at the position $(1,0)$ when $t=0,$ find the position function of the particle.",
      "worked_solution": "The position function of a particle moving in a circular path of radius $R$ in the $xy$-plane with a constant angular velocity $\\omega $ is given by\n\n$$\nr(t)=R(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t\\,j),\n$$\n\nwhere it is assumed that the circle is centered at $O,$ and the particle is at the position $(R,0)$ when $t=0.$\n\nSince the object's initial position is $(1,0),$ we have that $r(0)=i,$ and we can conclude that the circle's radius is $R=1.$\n\nTherefore, since we have $R=1$ and $\\omega =\\frac{1}{4}\\text{ rad/s},$ we get that the position function is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\frac{t}{4}\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{t}{4}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
