    "q-97566": {
      "dom_id": "step-q97566",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "A particle $P$ moves along a counterclockwise circular path centered at $O$ in the $xy$-plane with a constant angular velocity of $4\\,\\text{rad/s}.$ Given that the particle is located at $(2,0)$ when $t=0,$ find the velocity of the particle at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ seconds.",
      "worked_solution": "The position function of a particle moving in a circular path of radius $R$ in the $xy$-plane with a constant angular velocity $\\omega $ is given by\n\n$$\nr(t)=R(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t\\,j),\n$$\n\nwhere it is assumed that the circle is centered at $O,$ and the particle is at the position $(R,0)$ when $t=0.$\n\nIn our case, we have $R=2$ and $\\omega =4\\text{ rad/s},$ so we get that the position function is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =2(\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t\\,j).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe find the velocity vector by differentiating the position vector. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =(2(\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t\\,j))^{′} \\\\  & =-8\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t\\,i+8\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we find the velocity vector at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{4},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =-8\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4})\\,i+8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4})\\,j \\\\  & =-8\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi \\,i+8\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi \\,j \\\\  & =-8\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
